{"module":"twenty-twenties","voice":"female","duration":277.3,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"The 2020s: reckoning and backlash","start":0.0,"end":2.69,"words":[[0.05,0.19],[0.19,1.15],[1.39,1.87],[1.87,2.08],[2.08,2.49]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Many people believe the racial history in these modules is over.","start":3.49,"end":7.35,"words":[[3.54,3.82],[3.82,4.17],[4.17,4.51],[4.51,4.65],[4.65,5.06],[5.06,5.55],[5.55,5.69],[5.69,5.89],[5.89,6.38],[6.38,6.51],[6.51,6.86]]},{"el":"intro","text":"The 2020s show both how much it still shapes daily life and how quickly public attention can turn.","start":7.7,"end":14.2,"words":[[7.75,7.9],[7.9,8.85],[8.85,9.07],[9.07,9.37],[9.37,9.59],[9.59,9.88],[9.88,10.03],[10.03,10.32],[10.32,10.69],[10.69,11.06],[11.06,11.35],[11.35,11.57],[11.57,11.79],[11.79,12.23],[12.23,12.68],[12.68,13.19],[13.19,13.41],[13.41,13.71]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Several of these cases began with a call to police or a neighbor's suspicion.","start":14.55,"end":19.21,"words":[[14.55,15.0],[15.0,15.15],[15.15,15.37],[15.37,15.82],[15.82,16.2],[16.2,16.42],[16.42,16.57],[16.57,16.79],[16.79,16.94],[16.94,17.32],[17.32,17.39],[17.39,17.54],[17.54,17.99],[17.99,18.67]]},{"el":"h0","text":"2020","start":19.56,"end":20.67,"words":[[19.6,20.58]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Ahmaud Arbery was jogging in Brunswick, Georgia, in February 2020 when three white men decided he looked suspicious, chased him in pickup trucks and shot him.","start":21.37,"end":31.63,"words":[[21.43,21.72],[21.72,22.07],[22.07,22.29],[22.29,22.71],[22.71,22.86],[22.86,23.5],[23.75,24.25],[24.5,24.64],[24.64,25.21],[25.21,26.07],[26.07,26.28],[26.28,26.5],[26.5,26.78],[26.78,27.0],[27.0,27.57],[27.57,27.71],[27.71,28.0],[28.0,28.64],[28.89,29.32],[29.32,29.53],[29.53,29.67],[29.67,30.03],[30.03,30.39],[30.39,30.6],[30.6,30.81],[30.81,31.1]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Local prosecutors declined to charge them until a video surfaced.","start":31.98,"end":36.28,"words":[[32.03,32.43],[32.43,33.16],[33.16,33.69],[33.69,33.83],[33.83,34.16],[34.16,34.36],[34.36,34.69],[34.69,34.82],[34.82,35.29],[35.29,35.75]]},{"el":"s0","text":"All three were convicted of murder in 2021 and of federal hate crimes in 2022, and Georgia repealed its Civil War-era citizen's arrest law.","start":36.63,"end":46.78,"words":[[36.69,36.84],[36.84,37.06],[37.06,37.21],[37.21,37.89],[37.89,38.04],[38.04,38.34],[38.34,38.49],[38.49,39.62],[39.62,39.84],[39.84,40.0],[40.0,40.52],[40.52,40.82],[40.82,41.27],[41.27,41.42],[41.42,42.55],[42.81,43.04],[43.04,43.49],[43.49,43.94],[43.94,44.17],[44.17,44.54],[44.54,45.07],[45.07,45.67],[45.67,46.04],[46.04,46.27]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In March, Louisville police serving a no-knock warrant shot and killed Breonna Taylor in her apartment; the city then banned no-knock warrants.","start":47.13,"end":56.55,"words":[[47.18,47.34],[47.34,47.76],[48.05,48.63],[48.63,49.04],[49.04,49.45],[49.45,49.62],[49.62,50.12],[50.12,50.61],[50.61,50.86],[50.86,51.11],[51.11,51.44],[51.44,52.02],[52.02,52.44],[52.44,52.6],[52.6,52.77],[52.77,53.51],[53.8,53.97],[53.97,54.3],[54.3,54.55],[54.55,54.88],[54.88,55.38],[55.38,56.04]]},{"el":"s0","text":"On May 25, a store clerk called 911 about a suspected counterfeit $20 bill, and Minneapolis officer Derek Chauvin knelt on George Floyd's neck for more than nine minutes.","start":56.9,"end":69.11,"words":[[56.96,57.1],[57.1,57.32],[57.32,58.1],[58.35,58.49],[58.49,58.7],[58.7,58.99],[58.99,59.27],[59.27,60.62],[60.62,60.97],[60.97,61.11],[61.11,61.75],[61.75,62.46],[62.46,63.17],[63.17,63.46],[63.71,63.92],[63.92,64.7],[64.7,65.05],[65.05,65.41],[65.41,65.83],[65.83,66.12],[66.12,66.26],[66.26,66.61],[66.61,67.04],[67.04,67.25],[67.25,67.4],[67.4,67.54],[67.54,67.75],[67.75,68.03],[68.03,68.53]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Chauvin was convicted of murder in 2021.","start":69.46,"end":72.54,"words":[[69.51,69.88],[69.88,70.07],[70.07,70.63],[70.63,70.75],[70.75,71.0],[71.0,71.13],[71.13,72.13]]},{"el":"h1","text":"The largest protests in U.S. history","start":73.44,"end":75.87,"words":[[73.49,73.62],[73.62,74.05],[74.05,74.6],[74.6,74.73],[74.73,75.04],[75.35,75.78]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Surveys estimated that 15 million to 26 million Americans took part in protests in the weeks after Floyd's murder, in small towns as well as cities.","start":76.57,"end":87.61,"words":[[76.57,77.07],[77.07,77.9],[77.9,78.15],[78.15,78.65],[78.65,79.15],[79.15,79.31],[79.31,80.14],[80.14,80.64],[80.64,81.39],[81.39,81.64],[81.64,81.89],[81.89,82.05],[82.05,82.8],[82.8,82.97],[82.97,83.14],[83.14,83.47],[83.47,83.8],[83.8,84.3],[84.3,84.71],[85.01,85.17],[85.17,85.5],[85.5,85.92],[85.92,86.09],[86.09,86.33],[86.33,86.5],[86.5,87.0]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The House of Representatives passed the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act in 2020 and 2021; it never passed the Senate.","start":87.96,"end":96.48,"words":[[88.0,88.14],[88.14,88.43],[88.43,88.57],[88.57,89.58],[89.58,89.86],[89.86,90.01],[90.01,90.36],[90.36,90.72],[90.72,91.22],[91.22,91.37],[91.37,91.87],[91.87,92.08],[92.08,92.23],[92.23,93.08],[93.08,93.3],[93.3,94.44],[94.7,94.84],[94.84,95.12],[95.12,95.41],[95.41,95.55],[95.55,95.98]]},{"el":"s1","text":"A 2022 executive order set policing standards for federal agencies; it was revoked in 2025.","start":96.83,"end":104.5,"words":[[96.89,97.03],[97.03,98.02],[98.02,98.72],[98.72,98.94],[98.94,99.15],[99.15,99.64],[99.64,100.2],[100.2,100.34],[100.34,100.84],[100.84,101.54],[101.79,101.93],[101.93,102.14],[102.14,102.63],[102.63,102.78],[102.78,103.97]]},{"el":"s1","text":"New York repealed a law that had kept police disciplinary records secret and made it a civil rights violation to call police on someone falsely because of their race.","start":104.85,"end":114.71,"words":[[104.9,105.12],[105.12,105.34],[105.34,105.79],[105.79,105.94],[105.94,106.09],[106.09,106.32],[106.32,106.54],[106.54,106.84],[106.84,107.22],[107.22,108.04],[108.04,108.49],[108.49,108.94],[108.94,109.16],[109.16,109.46],[109.46,109.61],[109.61,109.76],[109.76,110.14],[110.14,110.51],[110.51,111.26],[111.26,111.41],[111.41,111.63],[111.63,112.01],[112.01,112.16],[112.16,112.61],[112.61,113.06],[113.06,113.43],[113.43,113.58],[113.58,113.8],[113.8,114.18]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Did the changes work?","start":115.61,"end":116.9,"words":[[115.65,115.8],[115.8,115.9],[115.9,116.35],[116.35,116.55]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Mapping Police Violence recorded more police killings in 2023 than in any year since it began tracking in 2013.","start":117.6,"end":125.78,"words":[[117.65,118.04],[118.04,118.43],[118.43,119.06],[119.06,119.6],[119.6,119.76],[119.76,120.15],[120.15,120.61],[120.61,120.77],[120.77,121.94],[121.94,122.17],[122.17,122.33],[122.33,122.56],[122.56,122.8],[122.8,123.11],[123.11,123.27],[123.27,123.66],[123.66,124.12],[124.12,124.28],[124.28,125.21]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Murders rose about 30% in 2020, the largest one-year increase on record, then fell sharply by 2024.","start":126.13,"end":134.71,"words":[[126.19,126.57],[126.57,126.88],[126.88,127.26],[127.26,128.03],[128.03,128.18],[128.18,129.18],[129.45,129.61],[129.61,130.15],[130.15,130.61],[130.61,131.07],[131.07,131.22],[131.22,131.68],[131.95,132.18],[132.18,132.41],[132.41,132.8],[132.8,133.03],[133.03,134.18]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Researchers still debate how much the pandemic, gun sales, changes in policing and the protests themselves contributed.","start":135.06,"end":142.85,"words":[[135.11,135.66],[135.66,135.94],[135.94,136.36],[136.36,136.56],[136.56,136.84],[136.84,136.98],[136.98,137.61],[137.85,138.06],[138.06,138.48],[138.72,139.34],[139.34,139.48],[139.48,139.97],[139.97,140.18],[140.18,140.32],[140.32,140.94],[140.94,141.5],[141.5,142.4]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Debates over “defunding” or reforming police split cities, some of which cut police budgets and then restored them.","start":143.2,"end":149.57,"words":[[143.25,143.72],[143.72,143.99],[143.99,144.53],[144.53,144.6],[144.6,145.07],[145.07,145.41],[145.41,145.75],[145.75,146.15],[146.39,146.59],[146.59,146.73],[146.73,147.0],[147.0,147.2],[147.2,147.54],[147.54,148.01],[148.01,148.21],[148.21,148.42],[148.42,148.82],[148.82,149.09]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Calls and suspicion that still turn deadly","start":150.47,"end":153.72,"words":[[150.49,150.89],[150.89,151.2],[151.2,152.0],[152.0,152.3],[152.3,152.71],[152.71,153.01],[153.01,153.51]]},{"el":"s3","text":"In January 2023, Memphis officers from a special unit beat Tyre Nichols after a traffic stop; he died three days later, and the unit was disbanded.","start":154.42,"end":164.07,"words":[[154.47,154.6],[154.6,155.2],[155.2,156.25],[156.48,156.88],[156.88,157.27],[157.27,157.54],[157.54,157.67],[157.67,158.07],[158.07,158.4],[158.4,158.59],[158.59,158.86],[158.86,159.25],[159.25,159.52],[159.52,159.65],[159.65,160.05],[160.05,160.38],[160.61,160.74],[160.74,161.0],[161.0,161.2],[161.2,161.46],[161.46,161.86],[162.09,162.29],[162.29,162.42],[162.42,162.75],[162.75,162.95],[162.95,163.61]]},{"el":"s3","text":"In April 2023, 16-year-old Ralph Yarl was shot in Kansas City after ringing the wrong doorbell to pick up his brothers; he survived.","start":164.42,"end":172.74,"words":[[164.48,164.61],[164.61,165.01],[165.01,166.08],[166.31,167.31],[167.31,167.58],[167.58,167.78],[167.78,167.98],[167.98,168.18],[168.18,168.31],[168.31,168.71],[168.71,168.98],[168.98,169.24],[169.24,169.58],[169.58,169.71],[169.71,169.91],[169.91,170.24],[170.24,170.38],[170.38,170.58],[170.58,170.71],[170.71,170.91],[170.91,171.38],[171.61,171.74],[171.74,172.28]]},{"el":"s3","text":"In June 2023, Ajike Owens was shot through a neighbor's door in Florida after a dispute over children playing; the neighbor was convicted of manslaughter.","start":173.09,"end":182.4,"words":[[173.14,173.28],[173.28,173.55],[173.55,174.62],[174.86,175.26],[175.26,175.59],[175.59,175.8],[175.8,176.0],[176.0,176.2],[176.2,176.33],[176.33,176.74],[176.74,176.87],[176.87,177.01],[177.01,177.48],[177.48,177.74],[177.74,177.88],[177.88,178.35],[178.35,178.62],[178.62,179.16],[179.16,179.63],[179.86,180.0],[180.0,180.33],[180.33,180.53],[180.53,181.14],[181.14,181.27],[181.27,181.88]]},{"el":"s3","text":"In July 2024, Sonya Massey called 911 for help about a possible prowler, and an Illinois deputy who responded shot her in her own kitchen; he was convicted of second-degree murder in 2025.","start":182.75,"end":196.42,"words":[[182.8,182.94],[182.94,183.36],[183.36,184.39],[184.63,184.97],[184.97,185.25],[185.25,185.53],[185.53,186.83],[186.83,186.97],[186.97,187.25],[187.25,187.59],[187.59,187.73],[187.73,188.21],[188.21,188.69],[188.94,189.14],[189.14,189.28],[189.28,189.69],[189.69,190.18],[190.18,190.31],[190.31,190.93],[190.93,191.14],[191.14,191.28],[191.28,191.42],[191.42,191.55],[191.55,191.76],[191.76,192.24],[192.48,192.62],[192.62,192.83],[192.83,193.45],[193.45,193.59],[193.59,194.34],[194.34,194.62],[194.62,194.76],[194.76,195.93]]},{"el":"s3","text":"The contested deaths page tracks disputed hanging deaths that continue today.","start":196.77,"end":201.78,"words":[[196.82,196.96],[196.96,197.62],[197.62,197.91],[197.91,198.28],[198.28,198.64],[198.64,199.3],[199.3,199.66],[199.66,199.95],[199.95,200.17],[200.17,200.76],[200.76,201.19]]},{"el":"h4","text":"The backlash","start":202.68,"end":203.76,"words":[[202.73,202.94],[202.94,203.54]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Since 2021, more than a dozen states have passed laws or policies restricting how teachers can discuss race and racism.","start":204.46,"end":212.78,"words":[[204.46,204.77],[204.77,205.98],[206.24,206.39],[206.39,206.62],[206.62,206.77],[206.77,207.15],[207.15,207.6],[207.6,207.83],[207.83,208.13],[208.13,208.36],[208.36,208.43],[208.43,208.96],[208.96,209.72],[209.72,209.94],[209.94,210.4],[210.4,210.62],[210.62,211.08],[211.08,211.38],[211.38,211.61],[211.61,212.29]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Florida rejected a pilot AP African American Studies course in 2023.","start":213.13,"end":218.62,"words":[[213.18,213.68],[213.68,214.33],[214.33,214.47],[214.47,214.91],[214.91,215.05],[215.05,215.55],[215.55,216.13],[216.13,216.56],[216.56,216.78],[216.78,216.92],[216.92,218.07]]},{"el":"s4","text":"That June, the Supreme Court ended race-conscious college admissions in Students for Fair Admissions v. Harvard.","start":218.97,"end":226.21,"words":[[219.03,219.25],[219.25,219.63],[219.89,220.04],[220.04,220.49],[220.49,220.71],[220.71,221.09],[221.09,221.84],[221.84,222.28],[222.28,222.88],[222.88,223.03],[223.03,223.71],[223.71,223.86],[223.86,224.08],[224.08,224.68],[224.68,224.9],[225.28,225.73]]},{"el":"s4","text":"In January 2025, executive orders ended federal diversity, equity and inclusion programs, and many companies scaled back their own.","start":226.56,"end":237.12,"words":[[226.61,226.76],[226.76,227.44],[227.44,228.73],[228.99,229.75],[229.75,230.05],[230.05,230.43],[230.43,230.96],[230.96,231.71],[231.98,232.43],[232.43,232.66],[232.66,233.26],[233.26,234.02],[234.28,234.51],[234.51,234.81],[234.81,235.41],[235.41,235.87],[235.87,236.09],[236.09,236.32],[236.32,236.62]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Supporters call these changes a return to colorblind rules; opponents say they erase history and remove tools for addressing discrimination that still exists.","start":237.47,"end":247.59,"words":[[237.51,238.04],[238.04,238.27],[238.27,238.49],[238.49,239.18],[239.18,239.33],[239.33,239.71],[239.71,239.86],[239.86,240.62],[240.62,241.0],[241.27,241.95],[241.95,242.18],[242.18,242.41],[242.41,242.79],[242.79,243.32],[243.32,243.54],[243.54,243.92],[243.92,244.23],[244.23,244.38],[244.38,244.91],[244.91,245.97],[245.97,246.2],[246.2,246.51],[246.51,247.11]]},{"el":"h5","text":"What's moving now","start":248.49,"end":249.77,"words":[[248.54,248.91],[248.91,249.38],[249.38,249.66]]},{"el":"s5","text":"The CROWN Act, which bans discrimination based on natural hair texture and protective styles such as braids and locs, has passed in more than 20 states since California's in 2019; the House passed a federal version in 2022.","start":250.47,"end":265.87,"words":[[250.51,250.65],[250.65,251.02],[251.02,251.31],[251.57,251.86],[251.86,252.15],[252.15,253.18],[253.18,253.54],[253.54,253.69],[253.69,254.28],[254.28,254.5],[254.5,255.01],[255.01,255.23],[255.23,255.89],[255.89,256.32],[256.32,256.62],[256.62,256.76],[256.76,257.2],[257.2,257.42],[257.42,257.79],[258.04,258.26],[258.26,258.56],[258.56,258.7],[258.7,258.85],[258.85,259.07],[259.07,259.51],[259.51,259.95],[259.95,260.24],[260.24,260.97],[260.97,261.12],[261.12,262.14],[262.4,262.54],[262.54,262.84],[262.84,263.13],[263.13,263.28],[263.28,263.79],[263.79,264.15],[264.15,264.3],[264.3,265.4]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Cities from Evanston to Tulsa are experimenting with repair.","start":266.22,"end":269.99,"words":[[266.25,266.6],[266.6,266.87],[266.87,267.43],[267.43,267.56],[267.56,267.91],[267.91,267.98],[267.98,268.87],[268.87,269.08],[269.08,269.49]]},{"el":"s5","text":"And CAREN-style laws are exactly the kind of local and state win this campaign is built to spread.","start":270.34,"end":276.36,"words":[[270.39,270.61],[270.61,271.34],[271.34,271.56],[271.56,271.63],[271.63,272.22],[272.22,272.36],[272.36,272.73],[272.73,272.87],[272.87,273.31],[273.31,273.53],[273.53,273.9],[273.9,274.12],[274.12,274.34],[274.34,274.85],[274.85,275.0],[275.0,275.29],[275.29,275.44],[275.44,275.88]]}]}